Who sees it: uploads are public at once. ExoFOP offers a 12-month proprietary period only to members of the TESS Follow-up Observing Program Working Group (TFOP WG), so upload after the Zenodo record is published.

## Step 3. {{ titles["3"] }}

Accounts: an AAS journals account (the submission system of the Research Notes of the AAS) and an arXiv account. A first submission to astro-ph.EP may need an endorsement from someone who has already posted there; arXiv tells you when you submit, and the endorsement request goes by email to a colleague who can endorse. The engine cannot submit for you.

The limits (AAS research note guidelines): at most {{ "{:,}".format(f.limits.total) }} words including the title, headings, caption and references, of which up to {{ f.limits.abstract }} are the required abstract, and one figure or one table, not both. The draft is `note/note.tex`, with one figure, `note/figure1`: {{ f.note_words.total }} words in all ({{ f.note_words.body }} of title, headings, text and caption, {{ f.note_words.abstract }} of abstract, {{ f.note_words.references }} of references; the author block and keywords are not counted).
{% if f.note_problems %}
**Over the limit:** {{ f.note_problems | join("; ") }}. Shorten it before you submit.
{% endif %}

1. Fill in the author block (affiliation, email, ORCID) and add co-authors.
{% if f.zenodo and f.zenodo.doi and f.zenodo.sandbox %}2. Replace {{ f.zenodo.doi }} (a sandbox DOI) before submission: use the DOI of the record you publish on zenodo.org in step 1.{% elif f.zenodo and f.zenodo.doi %}2. Check that {{ f.zenodo.doi }}, the draft's reserved DOI, matches the published record.{% else %}2. Replace {{ f.doi_shown }} with the Zenodo DOI from step 1.{% endif %}{{ "" }}
3. Read every sentence against `dossier.html`; the note is built from the stored numbers and says nothing the dossier does not.
4. Compile it with AASTeX v7 (aastex7.cls) and pdflatex; Overleaf has the AAS template. The UAT keywords can be changed in the submission form. {% if f.png %}The figure is `note/figure1.pdf`.{% else %}matplotlib could not be imported when this pack was built, so there is no PDF figure: convert `note/figure1.svg` to PDF first (Inkscape: `inkscape figure1.svg --export-type=pdf`).{% endif %}

5. Submit it as a Research Note of the AAS. The Note is moderated by an editor for fit, not refereed, and it gets a DOI when published.
6. After acceptance, post the same text to arXiv in astro-ph.EP.

## Step 4. {{ titles["4"] }}

Account: none beyond an email address. The NASA Exoplanet Archive takes messages through its help desk form ({{ f.helpdesk_url }}). The engine cannot send it.

When: only once a refereed paper on this candidate is accepted. The archive takes planet parameters from accepted refereed papers, so it adds objects from a refereed paper, not from the Research Note: the Note gives a DOI and a citable ephemeris, but alone it does not open this route. When the paper is accepted, paste this paragraph (also in `archive_email.txt`), with the DOIs filled in:

